{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## INDEPENDENT AC RE-VERIFICATION (2nd pass, post-1302/1303/1305): 17 of 18 MET, CRITERION 11 IS NOT\n\nCommissioned a second read-only pass over all 18 criteria against the tree and harness run\n**30840572608** (job 91776309249, `collected=58 executed=57 skipped=1`, 6 failed / 51 passed /\n1 xfailed) — not against this ticket's summaries of itself.\n\n**MET: 17** (1-10, 12-18). **NOT MET: 1** (criterion 11). **Cannot verify: 0.**\n\nHighlights worth recording rather than re-deriving later:\n * **Criterion 10's vacuity is genuinely gone.** The `08-assign` truthiness oracle comment 31 found\n   is fixed: both `test_the_inbound_assignee_mints_a_jira_family_identity` and\n   `test_inbound_assign_round_trips` now assert an empty-first SETUP and pass non-vacuously.\n * **Criterion 12's positive control landed** — the idempotence cell now asserts the edit actually\n   landed and waits for the index, closing comment 31's flagged gap.\n * **Criterion 13 is no longer self-referential** — the pagination precondition uses raw-REST\n   `raw_indexed_issue_count` instead of measuring itself with the code under test.\n * **Criteria 2, 3 and 18 remain WEAK, unchanged from comment 31**: each re-reads a value the same\n   fixture set moments earlier (`conftest.py:620`, `:624-625`), so they catch stray ambient state\n   but cannot verify the fixture's own logic. Recorded, not fixed — no product behaviour rests on\n   them.\n\n### ONE VERIFIER CLAIM WAS WRONG, AND I CHECKED IT RATHER THAN RECORDING IT\n\nThe pass reported that 88d9's inbound-parent-clear fix \"was reverted by `2241e3d189`, so the gap is\nnow structural\" and flagged it as a material finding. **That is incorrect.** It saw the revert and\nmissed the re-land. Verified directly:\n\n    25ead49f3e  \"Clear a Jira-dropped parent only on peer evidence\"   <- ON gerrit/main\n    binding_store.py:478,494   get_peer_parent / set_peer_parent      <- present\n    inbound_differ.py:242-247  reads get_peer_parent (getattr-guarded for legacy stores)\n    inbound_fields.py:307,348  diff_inbound_parent(peer_parent=...) → `if not peer_parent:` declines\n\nThe evidence-gated clear is intact. `test_inbound_clear_parent_round_trips` is red for the reason\nalready filed as [rebar:37e7-d751-0042-4b94] — DC REFUSES to null a sub-task's parent, reported as\nSETUP FAILED — not because the fix is absent.\n\n(My own first grep for `get_peer_parent` in `inbound_fields.py` returned zero and briefly looked\nalarming; the parameter there is spelled `peer_parent` and the accessor call lives in\n`inbound_differ.py`. A name-shaped grep is not a reference search — the repo's own code-navigation\nguidance says exactly this.)\n\n### CRITERION 11 — NOT MET, and it is now THE blocker for this ticket and the epic\n\nFive cells red on run 30840572608, every one a FILED product or platform defect:\n\n    test_outbound_create_stamps_both_provenance_markers   [rebar:18a5-2bd8-3e56-4bd8]  (root-caused)\n    test_outbound_set_subtask_parent_round_trips          [rebar:1a9f-50c0-e7a5-4fda]\n    test_inbound_set_subtask_parent_round_trips           [rebar:1a9f-50c0-e7a5-4fda]\n    test_inbound_clear_parent_round_trips                 [rebar:37e7-d751-0042-4b94]  (platform)\n    test_outbound_clear_parent_round_trips                this epic's 39c1 — fix in Gerrit 1311\n\n`test_inbound_delete_link_round_trips` is correctly XFAIL by design (1303), not a failure.\n\n**Also confirmed: the AC text still literally prescribes `pytest.raises(NotImplementedError)` for\nrow 12's epic case**, which Gerrit 1311 inverts. My earlier comment recorded a *proposed* amendment\nfor the operator; it remains unapplied, so the AC and the code now disagree in writing.\n\n### THE DECISION THIS FORCES — stated plainly rather than resolved unilaterally\n\nCriterion 11 as written requires every mutation to **round-trip**. Read literally, 5200 cannot close\nuntil 18a5, 1a9f and 37e7 are all fixed — which pulls three freshly-filed defects (one of them a\nplatform constraint rebar cannot fix) onto epic e369's critical path.\n\nThat reading is in tension with how this story has operated throughout: **every product bug the\nsuite found was filed separately and 5200 continued** — 8d68, 751e, 2b16, 88d9, 39c1 all followed\nthat pattern, and 5200's stated purpose is to BUILD the comprehensive live suite, not to fix\neverything it finds.\n\nThe competing consideration is the operator's earlier ruling on this very criterion: the row-12\ngap was to be **BUILT, not amended away**. That ruling was about a COVERAGE gap. What is left now is\nnot missing coverage — the cells exist, execute, and correctly report red — it is unfixed PRODUCT\nbehaviour they have surfaced.\n\n**I am not amending criterion 11 on my own authority**, because it is the one criterion this ticket\nhas already had an operator ruling on. Recorded for decision."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785787021355454001,"uuid":"1ba8111a-ff08-4c76-80c5-518b5a4ff288"}